# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Identifiers that are still pending, and why.
#
# This block is the state of the record, not a note to self. Anyone citing
# TopoTrail should know which parts of the citation are provisional.
#
# 1. ORCID of the author — NOT YET REGISTERED.
#    The `orcid:` line under `authors:` is kept commented out, and deliberately
#    so: the CFF schema accepts any string of the right shape, so a placeholder
#    would validate while resolving to a different person, or to nobody. Register
#    free at https://orcid.org, then uncomment the line and paste the real
#    identifier — that is the only edit needed.
#
# 2. Version DOI for 1.3.0 — DOES NOT EXIST YET.
#    Zenodo mints a version DOI only when the corresponding GitHub release is
#    published. The newest version DOI recorded under `identifiers:` is therefore
#    still the one for 1.1.2, and it is labelled as such: it is NOT the DOI of the
#    version this file declares. To close this: tag `v1.3.0`, publish the release,
#    let Zenodo archive it, then add the new version DOI and release URL to
#    `identifiers:` and update `README.md` and `paper.md` with them.
#
#    The concept DOI in `doi:` never changes and always resolves to the most
#    recent archived version, so a citation of this file is never broken — only
#    less precise than it will be once the release exists.
#
# Authorship is settled: one author. The JOSS criterion is substantial
# contribution to the software itself, and the whole commit history is the
# author's. Leandro Freitas supervised the research of which this software is a
# product, which is an acknowledgement and not software authorship; that
# acknowledgement belongs in `paper.md`, and is there.
#
# Citation form used by the author in the literature: MACIEL, L. S. C.
# The contact address is the project's, not a personal one, so it survives
# changes of institution and can be answered by whoever maintains the tool.
#
# On every new release, update `version`, `date-released` and the version DOI in
# `identifiers:`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TopoTrail: a QGIS plugin for DEM-based topographic suitability and least-cost route planning"
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Luan da Silva Cortes"
    family-names: "Maciel"
    alias: "MACIEL, L. S. C."
    email: "herpetomantiqueira@gmail.com"
    # TO BE FILLED IN — see note 1 at the top of this file. Uncomment and paste
    # the real identifier once registered; do not substitute a placeholder.
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/____-____-____-____"
    affiliation: "Escola Nacional de Botânica Tropical, Instituto de Pesquisas Jardim Botânico do Rio de Janeiro, Brazil"
contact:
  - given-names: "Luan da Silva Cortes"
    family-names: "Maciel"
    email: "herpetomantiqueira@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/LuanCortesM/Topotrail"
url: "https://plugins.qgis.org/plugins/TopoTrail/"
abstract: >-
  TopoTrail is a QGIS plugin that supports preliminary planning of trails,
  access routes and field corridors in natural and protected areas. From a
  single Digital Elevation Model it derives slope, curvature, ruggedness, a
  topographic wetness index and the drainage network, models topographic
  suitability by weighted multicriteria analysis, and produces a relative
  topographic risk surface, a transitability map in five absolute slope classes,
  potential access zones, a least-cost route costed as walking time through
  Tobler's anisotropic hiking function, a metric corridor around that route, and
  the watercourse crossings the route makes, each graded by contributing area and
  flagged for field checking. Every run writes a JSON diagnostic log recording
  the versions, the parameters and the statistics of every intermediate raster.
  Results are decision-support evidence and require field validation.
keywords:
  - QGIS
  - GIS
  - digital elevation model
  - multicriteria analysis
  - least-cost path
  - Tobler hiking function
  - trail planning
  - protected areas
  - geomorphometry
license: MIT
# Concept DOI: always resolves to the latest archived version. Never changes.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20295565"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.20295565"
    description: "Concept DOI for all versions of TopoTrail (Zenodo)"
  # PENDING: there is no version DOI for 1.3.0 yet. The two entries below are the
  # newest that exist, and they are for 1.1.2 — an earlier version with different
  # numerical results. See note 2 at the top of this file.
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.22399472"
    description: "Version DOI for TopoTrail 1.1.2 (Zenodo) — NOT the version declared below; the 1.3.0 version DOI is pending its release"
  - type: url
    value: "https://github.com/LuanCortesM/Topotrail/releases/tag/v1.1.2"
    description: "GitHub release v1.1.2 — the most recent tag; v1.3.0 is not tagged yet"
version: "1.3.0"
date-released: "2026-09-13"
